    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pstagz7",
      "content": "The frequency of a sound wave is 500 Hz and its wavelength is 0.68 m. The speed of sound is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "hocx78d",
      "content": "A) 300 m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "2yfdqqf",
      "content": "B) 320 m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "496memi",
      "content": "C) 340 m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "n751a99",
      "content": "D) 360 m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "xayif3j",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: C (340 m/s)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9tf7th9",
      "content": "Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kj9u29e",
      "content": "Step 1: Use wave equation."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "jbrtayo",
      "content": "v = fλ"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l5v5r0x",
      "content": "Step 2: Substitute given values."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "v02oy8d",
      "content": "v = 500 × 0.68"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "h68j4r8",
      "content": "Step 3: Multiply carefully."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "h3t2pv0",
      "content": "v = 340 m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "d3xfi6w",
      "content": "Final Answer = 340 m/s"
    },
    {
      "id": "34rjve4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q2."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "l5exjyf",
      "content": "An echo is heard after 0.2 seconds. If speed of sound is 340 m/s, distance of reflecting surface is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "jrzkjjo",
      "content": "A) 17 m"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "bz97fvs",
      "content": "B) 34 m"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "nq4f6mj",
      "content": "C) 68 m"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "iq1sklf",
      "content": "D) 85 m"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "vgyw2z1",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: B (34 m)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lexu991",
      "content": "Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7dmajxp",
      "content": "Step 1: Use formula for echo distance."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mnjm45g",
      "content": "Distance = (v × t) / 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "msjm21u",
      "content": "Step 2: Substitute values."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "MCQs",
      "id": "7cy4hhw"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nvu6l0g",
      "content": "Distance = (340 × 0.2) / 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "biqsppe",
      "content": "= 68 / 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "lhy76hp",
      "content": "= 34 m"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ukodwjv",
      "content": "Division by 2 because sound travels to surface and back."
    },
    {
      "id": "v5rrg2z",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q3."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kx23h96",
      "content": "Two tuning forks of frequencies 256 Hz and 260 Hz are sounded together. Number of beats per second is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "do7npny",
      "content": "A) 2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "fsoeygy",
      "content": "B) 3"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "15ulsk0",
      "content": "C) 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "9tq73oc",
      "content": "D) 6"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "mjzihmk",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: C (4)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "si4g5fb",
      "content": "Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4ogm3qs",
      "content": "Formula: Beats per second = |f1 - f2|"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "hyj2fzv",
      "content": "= |260 - 256|"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "7dxuvkn",
      "content": "= 4 beats per second"
    },
    {
      "id": "w9sp61u",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q4."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2z4pjsr",
      "content": "Find speed of sound at 30°C. (Use v = 331 + 0.6T)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "al2vdq4",
      "content": "A) 331 m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "x0c9z14",
      "content": "B) 343 m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "qih3t15",
      "content": "C) 349 m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "0ds0lti",
      "content": "D) 360 m/s"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "vesakt4",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: C (349 m/s)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "479n28x",
      "content": "Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7e8vrtg",
      "content": "Step 1: Use formula."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "yc4mgg8",
      "content": "v = 331 + 0.6T"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xk4cs3v",
      "content": "Step 2: Substitute T = 30°C"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pprj5g2",
      "content": "v = 331 + (0.6 × 30)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "1ckiuyx",
      "content": "= 331 + 18"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "q47kxrn",
      "content": "= 349 m/s"
    },
    {
      "id": "modqcal",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Q5."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7bbhxps",
      "content": "If amplitude of a sound wave becomes twice, intensity becomes:"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Multiple Choice Questions require high accuracy and time management during competitive examinations.",
        "Regular practice of objective question sets helps eliminate options systematically."
      ],
      "id": "dr4l9ru"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "9c29lmo",
      "content": "A) Same"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "jjw9pbg",
      "content": "B) Two times"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "0v6bby5",
      "content": "C) Four times"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "rz31jk2",
      "content": "D) Eight times"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "x7vthqc",
      "content": "<br></br>Correct Answer: C (Four times)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x67udfk",
      "content": "Detailed Solution:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "4f0h94m",
      "content": "Intensity ∝ Amplitude²"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "v02gtk4",
      "content": "If amplitude becomes 2A:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "6jxf8yi",
      "content": "New intensity ∝ (2A)²"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "zpeebf9",
      "content": "= 4A²"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pmb51me",
      "content": "Therefore, intensity becomes four times."
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}